message: "If you use this software, please cite both the article and the software release."
title: "Data-Centric Trust Pipeline: Reference Implementation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cavalcanti Pereira"
    given-names: "Carlos Diego"
    affiliation: "Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Sloan School of Management (Visiting Fellows Program); CESAR School, Recife, Brazil"
    email: "cdiego@mit.edu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2003-8713"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the Data-Centric Trust Pipeline — a four-layer
  governance framework (Integrity, Fairness, Synthesis, Provenance) for
  trustworthy AI in sensitive domains. Includes empirical validation on the
  Adult Census Income and ProPublica COMPAS datasets across 32 dataset-
  generator-seed configurations (26 independent pipeline executions),
  the four-protocol validation structure for synthetic data (P1
  distributional invariance, P2 fairness delta as batch-level discriminators;
  P3 cryptographic provenance, P4 domain plausibility as record-level
  invariants), three specified conflict-resolution protocols, and a
  decision-level provenance graph with auditable rationale records.
keywords:
  - trustworthy AI
  - data governance
  - algorithmic fairness
  - synthetic data
  - data provenance
  - accountability
  - data-centric AI
  - AI auditing
  - decision-level provenance
